==Description== <!--T:3-->

<!--T:14-->
The '''Std Refresh''' command recomputes selected objects ({{Version|26.3}}), or the active document if no objects are selected. The command is disabled if no recompute is required, but in that case the command can still be invoked through its shortcut.

==Usage== <!--T:5-->

<!--T:7-->
# There are several ways to invoke the command:
#* Press the {{Button|[[Image:Std_Refresh.svg|16px]] [[Std_Refresh|Recompute]]}} button.
#* Select the {{MenuCommand|Edit → [[Image:Std_Refresh.svg|16px]] Recompute}} option from the menu.
#* Use the keyboard shortcut: {{KEY|Ctrl}}+{{KEY|Shift}}+{{KEY|R}}.

==Options== <!--T:15-->

<!--T:16-->
* If no recompute is required and the command is disabled, a recompute can be forced:
*# In the [[Tree_View|Tree View]]:
*#* Select one or more individual objects.
*#* Select the document to include all objects.
*# Select the {{MenuCommand|[[Image:Std_MarkToRecompute.svg|16px]] Mark to Recompute}} option from the context menu.
*# Invoke the now enabled command as described above.
* Alternatively, to recompute individual objects:
*# Select one or more individual objects in the [[Tree_View|Tree View]]
*# Select the {{MenuCommand|[[Image:Std_Refresh.svg|16px]] Recompute Object}} from the context menu.

==Notes== <!--T:17-->

<!--T:18-->
* For a macro that will recompute the active document see: [[Macro_ForceRecompute|Macro ForceRecompute]].

==Scripting== <!--T:10-->

<!--T:11-->
See also: [https://freecad.github.io/SourceDoc/ Autogenerated API documentation] and [[FreeCAD_Scripting_Basics|FreeCAD Scripting Basics]].

<!--T:12-->
To recompute a document use the {{incode|recompute}} method of the document object.

</translate>
{{Code|code=
import FreeCAD

doc = FreeCAD.ActiveDocument
doc.recompute()
}}
<translate>

If an object is not updated by this method, it may help to mark the object as touched, which corresponds to '''Mark to recompute''', using the {{incode|touch}} method of the object before using document recompute.

</translate>
{{Code|code=
obj.touch()
}}
<translate>

To recompute an individual object use the {{incode| recompute}} method of the object.

</translate>
{{Code|code=
obj.recompute()
}}
<translate>

===Examples===

This corresponds to selecting the document and invoking this command, see [[#Options|Options]]:

</translate>
{{Code|code=
import FreeCAD

doc = FreeCAD.ActiveDocument
for obj in doc.Objects:
    obj.touch()
doc.recompute()
}}
<translate>

This  corresponds to selecting the first 3 objects of the document and invoking '''Recompute Object''' from the context menu, see [[#Options|Options]]:

</translate>
{{Code|code=
import FreeCAD

doc = FreeCAD.ActiveDocument
for obj in doc.Objects[0:3]:
    obj.recompute()
}}
